---
/**
 * The price, on `/pricing`.
 *
 * ── It was four plans and a calculator until 2026-09-08 ──
 * The tiers differed in exactly one thing: a higher monthly fee bought a lower per-sale commission.
 * The commission went when the seller started clearing into his OWN account (`docs/pivot-saas.md`)
 * — the buyer's money never passes through us, so there is nothing to take a percentage of — and
 * with it the ladder had no dimension left. Four prices for one product is a page where every
 * reader picks the cheapest, and a "which plan is right for you" calculator that can only ever
 * answer "the 99₪ one" is a decision aid for a decision that no longer exists.
 *
 * **What that removed is worth naming, because each piece was there for a reason:** a revenue field
 * the reader typed his own number into, a cheapest-plan badge that moved as he typed, a saving line
 * ("Growth saves you 500₪ a month" — exact, because the clearing fee is identical on every plan and
 * cancels in a difference), the four cards, and the signed-in flow that let a seller choose from
 * here and have `/api/seller/tier` amend his standing order. All of it answered "which one", and
 * there is no "which one".
 *
 * **What deliberately did NOT come back:** a monthly TOTAL. The owner ruled it out on 2026-08-24
 * (*"לא צריך להראות למוכר כמה הוא ישלם לנו בחודש עם המכירות, זה רעיון גרוע, זה נראה מפחיד"*) and
 * the reasoning survives the simplification — a bill he has not earned yet, standing beside the
 * subscription as if the subscription had been a lie. With one plan the price IS the total, which
 * is the same rule reached from the other side.
 *
 * The four `p.tiers` entries stay in the copy: `resolveTier` still answers for stored ids from the
 * four-tier era, and a name for each is what keeps an old `stores.tier` value renderable.
 */
import { SELLER_TIERS, SELLER_SETUP_FEE } from '../lib/pricing.js';
import type { getT } from '../i18n/index.js';

interface Props {
  p: ReturnType<typeof getT>['pricing'];
  lang: 'he' | 'en';
  /** Only a signed-in seller is told where a choice would land — for a visitor the same button is a
   *  redirect to registration, and a line naming a dashboard tab he has no account for is noise. */
  isLoggedIn: boolean;
}
const { p, isLoggedIn } = Astro.props;

const plan = SELLER_TIERS[0]!;
---

{/* One price, stated once. No grid: a single card in a four-column layout reads as three cards
    that failed to load, and a lone card centred in an empty row is a shape this site does not use
    anywhere else. It is a panel the width of the prose above it. */}
<div class="pricing-panel mt-4" data-tier={plan.id}>
  <p class="m-0 flex items-baseline gap-1.5 flex-wrap">
    <span class="text-[2rem] font-bold tabular-nums">₪{plan.monthlyFee}</span>
    <span class="muted text-[0.9rem]">{p.perMonth}</span>
    <span class="muted text-[0.9rem]">· {p.vatNote}</span>
  </p>
  {/* The plan's NAME ("בסיס") is not printed. It was the label that told four cards apart, and with
      one price it names nothing — a heading over a single item. The id lives on in the data because
      stored `stores.tier` rows still carry it. */}
  <p class="muted m-0 mt-2 text-[0.88rem] max-w-[46rem]">{p.sameEverything}</p>

  <button type="button" class="btn btn--accent mt-4" data-role="choose">{p.choose}</button>
</div>

{/* The facts that belong under a price and nowhere else on the page, in the order a reader asks
    them: per shop, what happens if he stops, when we start charging, and the one charge that is NOT
    the price — his processor's account-opening fee, which is his and was never ours.

    **Per shop** is a price fact a seller planning two shops has to have before he presses the
    button, not on the payment screen afterwards. **Cancelling** is here because the question that
    stops somebody pressing is not what it costs — it is what happens if he stops, and leaving that
    to a terms page is what makes a decision feel irreversible. */}
<p class="m-0 mt-3 text-[0.84rem] font-semibold">{p.perStore}</p>
<p class="muted m-0 mt-1 text-[0.82rem]">{p.cancelAny}</p>
<p class="muted m-0 mt-1 text-[0.82rem]">{p.whenBody}</p>
<p class="muted m-0 mt-1 text-[0.82rem]">{p.setupFee.replace('{amount}', String(SELLER_SETUP_FEE))}</p>

{/* Where a signed-in seller goes to actually start paying. Rendered as a plain link rather than
    filled by a script: with one plan the button above has nothing to save, so the page is the same
    cached document for everybody and the only per-seller fact left is whether he has an account. */}
{isLoggedIn && (
  <p class="m-0 mt-3 text-[0.88rem]">
    {p.savedWhere}{' '}<a href="/seller/dashboard?panel=payouts">{p.savedWhereLink}</a>
  </p>
)}
